========================================================================================
G079 -- THE COSMIC EQUIPARTITION BUDGET: what dark matter is, quantified
========================================================================================

========================================================================================
P1  THE DECOMPOSITION: Omega_dm/Omega_star ~ 100; equilibrium cannot close
========================================================================================
    Omega_dm           = 0.264   (Planck 2018/2020, published)
    Omega_star         = 0.0027  (Fukugita & Peebles 2004, published)
    Omega_dm/Omega_star = 97.8  ~ 100
    Omega_eq [uncapped 1:1 bound (stars + ISM gas)  ] = 0.0034  ->  1.28% of Omega_dm
    Omega_eq [capped at 0.62 M_b (registered cap, G03E)] = 0.0021  ->  0.79% of Omega_dm
    generous envelope (ALL cosmic baryons, no binding requirement): 18.7% -- NOT the law's bound (quoted to anchor the loosest reading)
    the equilibrium sector alone supplies 1/78 of the budget -- cannot close it; the remainder is the FREE DUST
  [PASS] G1 [decomposition] Omega_dm/Omega_star in the ~100 band (the task's honest ratio)
         measured: 97.8 (in [90, 110])
         reading : the 1:1 law binds the equilibrium sector to the baryons that generate it; the cosmic abundance of those baryons is the stellar density -- ratio ~ 98.
  [PASS] V1 [equipartition fraction] the equilibrium component is a sub-dominant fraction of Omega_dm (< 10%)
         measured: Omega_eq/Omega_dm = 0.79% (capped), 1.28% (uncapped) -- both < 10%
         reading : even the uncapped 1:1 bound (every galaxy dark mass = its baryon mass, plus ISM gas) is ~1.3%; the registered 0.62 cap (G03E) makes it ~0.8%.  The loosest conceivable reading (all cosmic baryons host sheets, no binding requirement) is 18.7% -- still sub-dominant, but it is NOT the law's bound and is quoted only to show the envelope.
  [PASS] V2 [free-dust share] the free-dust remainder carries > 90% of Omega_dm
         measured: dust share = 99.2% (capped bound) / 98.7% (uncapped bound); envelope reading 81.3%
         reading : stated honestly: with the law's own numbers (1:1 inside r_M, 0.62 cap) the equilibrium sector is ~1% and the free dust ~99%; even the uncapped bound gives > 98%.  The all-baryons envelope (81%) would fail the 90% bar but is not a bound of the committed law (the phantom is generated by the baryons BOUND in galaxies).

